 "response": "Kakir's budget is now **$1,075K**.\n\n**Approach**\n- **Only Finance Office budget entries count.** Messages from PMO, Sales, Legal, Engineering and other teams do not count. Finance Office entries that don't change the budget, such as audits, receipts and purchase orders, are also ignored.\n- **Withdrawal chains were followed to the end.** A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn is cancelled, and the update it targeted applies again. Examples:\n  - #0003 (\u2212$11K) **applies**. The chain is #0007 \u2192 #0111 \u2192 #0711 \u2192 #0956 \u2192 #1023 \u2192 #1039. #1039 cancels #1023, so #0956 stands, which leaves #0111 standing, which cancels #0007.\n  - #0005 (+$266K) is **withdrawn**. #0414 cancels #0073, so #0008's withdrawal of #0005 stands.\n  - #0078 (+$117K) **applies**. #0923 cancels #0348, so #0167 stands and cancels #0151's withdrawal.\n  - #0066 (\u2212$386K) is **withdrawn**. #1533 cancels #1470, so #1263's withdrawal stands.\n  - Similar chains decide #0010, #0030, #0039, #0060, #0062, #0112, #0176, #0198, #0261, #0406, #0463, #0539, #0852 (all withdrawn). They also decide #0024, #0124, #0172, #0213, #0280, #0378, #0410, #0519, #0603, #0630, #0635, #0881, #0884, #0900, #0910, #1041 (all apply).\n- **Calculation.** The budget starts at the $1,280K set in #0001. Every Finance Office change still in effect was then applied once, in record order. The running total ends at #1599 (\u2212$75K).\n\nANSWER: $1075K",
